feat(tui): model picker with pool, device panel, QR pairing, --connect

The TUI now shows what the cluster actually is, and can't overstate it.

Overlays:
- models (Up): pool size in GB above the list; D runs the model distributed
- devices (d): per-device budget, thread count, and whether it is genuinely
  usable. Unreachable peers are labelled NOT counted rather than silently
  inflating the pool.
- pairing (p): renders the scannable QR in the terminal plus the URI.

New flag: --connect <URL> attaches the UI to a node that is already running
(one node owns the port; a second terminal or another machine can still drive
it). Fails fast with an actionable message instead of showing an empty screen.

Honesty fixes found while testing the panels:
- peers were marked "stopped reporting" purely on heartbeat age, which showed
  a live worker as dead. Reachability is now probed and reported separately
  from staleness, and /peers exposes reachable + usable per device.
- the pool total counts only self + reachable peers. A device that reports RAM
  while nothing answers its RPC socket is excluded, with the reason shown.

verified in a real pty (rendered screen, not just logs):
- pairing overlay draws a 41x41 QR that OpenCV decodes back to the exact
  privateml:// URI including the real LAN IP 192.168.100.144
- devices overlay: "pool 12.8 GB usable across 3 device(s)", real worker
  marked reachable, unreachable peer marked NOT counted
- --connect against a live node prints the node identity; a dead address
  exits with a clear hint

tests: 27 passing
